TASK
Audit every number (currency, count, percentage, hours) in the business case and blueprint:
1. Does each trace to a client input above, or to shown arithmetic on those inputs?
2. Is the attribution present ("by your own figures", "at your planned $X")?
3. Are stated assumptions conservative and explicit? (Scenario fractions — conservative/expected/upside — are legitimate ONLY when explicitly labeled as assumptions and applied to client inputs with the arithmetic shown.)
4. Do any two statements give conflicting values or policies for the same fact (a cycle stated as both 2 days and monthly, two different volumes for the same operation)? A contradiction is a high finding.
5. Does any target percentage appear with no shown arithmetic and no named client input? Flag it.
6. RECOMPUTE every multiplication yourself — when an arithmetic string and its result both appear ("3 x $95 x 52 weeks = $19,000"), do the math. A wrong result is an invented figure wearing attribution: a high finding.
7. A scenario assumption may only be a rate or fraction applied to client inputs ("1 in 3 recovered"). Any absolute currency amount, wage, hours or margin the client never gave appearing as an assumption is a high finding — it belongs in missing_inputs instead.
8. BMV's own pricing must never appear anywhere — any fee, build price or session price of OURS is a high finding.
9. UNITS: verify every figure keeps its stated period (per day / week / month / year) in every appearance, and that annual claims state their basis (365-day year, 30-day operating month). Frequency drift on the same figure is a high finding.
10. THRESHOLDS: every accuracy %, SLA, evaluation window, sample size or rate in EITHER document that is not a client input must carry "(proposed — client approval required)" or equivalent. An unlabeled invented threshold is a high finding.
11. ONE BASE: the same computed quantity must use ONE value everywhere — a scenario computing from a base that differs from the stated canonical figure is a high finding.
List at most the 12 most material findings.
Ignore section numbering, page references and the client's own quoted answers.

Respond with ONLY this JSON shape, no markdown fences, no commentary:

